Q2: Kitne concurrent users expect kar rahe hain peak pe ? Peak pe kitni RPS aayegi ?
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Concurrent Users kya hai?

- Wo users jo ek specific moment pe system se actively connected hain — session active hai, requests bhej sakte hain.
- Example: 10M registered → 1M daily active → 100K peak concurrent users


RPS (Requests Per Second) kya hai?

- Ek second me system pe aane wali actual HTTP requests.
- RPS = Concurrent Users × Average Requests per User per Second
- Concurrent users se RPS directly nahi nikalta. Har user kitni requests/sec bhej raha hai — wo bhi chahiye.
- Example:
  Same concurrent users, different RPS possible:
  => 100K concurrent users, har user 1 req/min → 1,666 RPS
  => 100K concurrent users, har user 10 req/sec → 1M RPS
  => 100K concurrent users, har user 0.1 req/sec → 10K RPS


RPS se pata chalega counter Redis ki Capacity  i.e single Redis chalega ya redis cluster chahiye request counter ke liye .

Decision Formula

Single Redis chalega ya Cluster?

IF RPS <= 50,000  → Single Redis chalega ✅ 
IF RPS > 50,000   → Cluster chahiye ❌

Note: 

Har request ke required operations (GET, INCR, EXPIRE, ZADD, HGET, HMSET — jo bhi ho) Redis pe separate calls ke roop me nahi jaate. Generally ye saare operations 
ek single Lua script ke andar execute hote hain — atomicity ensure karne ke liye (race condition avoid karna, kyunki agar GET → CHECK → UPDATE alag calls hoti, to 
beech me doosri request interleave kar sakti thi).

Isliye capacity planning ke liye: 1 request = 1 Lua script = 1 Redis call = 1 Redis round trip 

Single Redis node capacity:
- Conservative: 50K ops/sec (safe)
- Actual: 80K-100K ops/sec tak handle kar sakta hai

Case-wise Design :

Case 1: Interviewer bole "10K RPS"

10,000 RPS < 50,000 → Single Redis chalega ✅

Design:
- Single Redis master
- 1 replica (HA ke liye — crash ho to promote ho jaye)
- Total: 2 Redis nodes


Case 2: Interviewer bole "100K RPS"

100,000 RPS > 50,000 → Cluster chahiye 

Design:
- Kitne nodes? = 100K / 50K = 2 nodes
- Headroom ke saath = 3 nodes (safe side)
- Each master + 1 replica
- Total: 6 Redis nodes (3 master + 3 replica)


Case 3: Interviewer bole "1M RPS"

1,000,000 RPS > 50,000 → Cluster chahiye 

Design:
- Kitne nodes? = 1M / 50K = 20 nodes
- Headroom ke saath = 25 nodes (safe side)
- Each master + 2 replicas
- Total: 75 Redis nodes (25 master + 50 replica)

